          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Rings of
            %em Witt vectors
            are the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/co-free+functor"} co-free
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lambda-rings"} Lambda-rings
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+number"} prime number
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            one speaks of
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                \-typical Witt vectors
            %em big Witt vectors
            if all primes are considered at once.
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arithmetic+geometry"} arithmetic geometry
            the impact of rings of Witt vectors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(R)
            of a given ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is that they are like rings
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+power+series"} formal power series
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec(R)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-adic+numbers"} p-adic numbers
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arithmetic+jet+space"} arithmetic jet space
            and at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Borger%27s+absolute+geometry"} Borger's absolute geometry
          %p
            In components, a
            %em Witt vector
            is an infinite sequence of elements of a given
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            structure on the set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(k)
            of Witt vectors of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(k)
            is therefore called
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                the Witt ring of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witt+polynomials"} Witt polynomials
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi w
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w_i
            for every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+number"} natural number
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic"} characteristic
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            the Witt ring of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            is sometimes called
            %em universal Witt ring
            to distinguish it from the case where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            is of prime characteristic and a similar but different construction is of interest.
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witt+vector"} p-adic Witt vector
            is an infinite sequence of elements af a commutative ring of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime"} prime
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic"} characteristic
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            except that only
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witt+polynomials"} Witt polynomials
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi w
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi p
                        %mi l
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w_{p^l}
            whose index is a power of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            are taken.
          %p
            More abstractly, the ring of Witt vectors carries the structure of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lambda-ring"} Lambda-ring
            and the construction
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi k
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W \colon k\mapsto W(k)
            of the Witt ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(k)
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
            from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lambda-rings"} Lambda-rings
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+rings"} commutative rings
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/co-free+functor"} co-free
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lambda-rings"} Lambda-rings
          %p
            Moreover
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(-)
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representable
            by ring of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+function"} symmetric functions
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Λ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Λ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda
            is the free Lambda-ring on the commutative ring
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Λ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Lambda
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hopf+algebra"} Hopf algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+scheme"} group scheme
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lambda-ring"} Lambda-ring
          %p
            The construction of Witt vectors gives a functorial way to lift a commutative ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime"} prime
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic"} characteristic
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            to a commutative ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(A)
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic"} characteristic
            0. Since this construction is functorial, it can be applied to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure+sheaf"} structure sheaf
            of an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+variety"} algebraic variety
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(A)
            has even more desirable properties: If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perfect+field"} perfect field
            then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(A)
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete-valuation+ring"} discrete valuation ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(A)
            involves a ring of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+series"} power series
            and a ring of power series over a field is always a discrete valuation ring.
          %p
            There is a generalization,
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W_G
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "#DS88"} DS88
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witt-Burnside+functors"} Witt-Burnside functor
          %p
            There is a generalization to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-commutative+Witt+vectors"} non-commutative Witt vectors
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lubin-Tate+ring"} Lubin-Tate ring
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lubin-Tate+theory"} Lubin-Tate theory
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomial+ring"} polynomial ring
            on a ring of Witt vectors and this way Witt vectors control much of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chromatic+homotopy+theory"} chromatic homotopy theory
          %h2#motivation Motivation
          %p
            In an
            %em expansion
            of a
            = succeed "-adic" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo =
                  %mi Σ
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mi i
                  %msup
                    %mi p
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a=\Sigma a_i p^i
            the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi a
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a^i
            are called
            = succeed "." do
              %em digits
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %mi p
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{0,1,\dots,p-1\}
          %p
            Equivalently the digits can be defined to be taken from the set
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mi p
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo ∪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_p:=\{x|x^{p-1}=1\}\cup \{0\}
            %em Teichmüller digits
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %em Teichmüller representatives
          %p
            The set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            is in bijection with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+field"} finite field
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(F_p)
            of (countably) infinite sequences of elements in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_p
            hence is in bijection to the set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_p
            of
            = succeed "-adic" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(F_p)
            called
            %em Witt ring structure
            such that all ‘’truncated expansion polynomials’‘
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Φ
                    %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi p
                        %mi n
                  %mo +
                  %mi p
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi p
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                  %mo +
                  %msup
                    %mi p
                    %mn 2
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi p
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mn 2
                  %mo +
                  %mi …
                  %mo +
                  %msup
                    %mi p
                    %mi n
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi_n=X^{p^n}+p X^{p^{n-1}}+p^2X^{p^{n-2}}+\dots +p^n X
            called
            %em Witt polynomials
            are morphisms
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Φ
                    %mi n
                  %mo :
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi_n:W(F_p)\to \mathbb{Z}_p
          %p of groups.
          %h2#Definituion Definition
          %p We first give the
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#DefinitionInComponents"} Explicit definition in components
          %p and then discuss the
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "DefinitionUniversalCharacterization"} Universal characterization
          %h3#DefinitionInComponents In components
          %h4#the_ring_structure The ring structure
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
            %p
              If the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic"} characteristic
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              is
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
              then the Witt ring
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(k)
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              is defined defined by the addition
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Σ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi Σ
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a_1, a_2, \ldots, )+(b_1, b_2, \ldots) :=(\Sigma_1(a_1,b_1), \Sigma_2(a_1,a_2,b_1,b_2), \ldots)
            %p and the multiplication
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a_1, a_2, \ldots )\cdot (b_1, b_2, \ldots ) :=(\Pi_1(a_1,b_1), \Pi_2(a_1,a_2,b_1,b_2), \ldots )
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              is of prime characteristic
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              we index the defining formulas by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi p
                      %mn 3
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^1,p^2,p^3,\dots
              instead of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 3
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1,2,3,\dots
            %p
              Here the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_i
              are called
              %em addition polynomials
              and the
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_i
              are called
              = succeed "," do
                %em multiplication polynomials
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#AdditionAndMultiplicationPolynomials"} below
          %h4#the_witt_polynomials_the__the__phantom_components
            The Witt polynomials, the
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_i
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_i
          %p
            let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_1, x_2, \ldots
            be a collection of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variables"} variables
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomial"} polynomial
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}[x_1, x_2, \ldots ]
            using the following formulas:
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi w
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w_1(X)=x_1
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi w
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msubsup
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                    %mn 2
                  %mo +
                  %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w_2(X)=x_1^2+2x_2
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi w
                    %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msubsup
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                    %mn 3
                  %mo +
                  %mn 3
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w_3(X)=x_1^3+3x_3
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi w
                    %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msubsup
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                    %mn 4
                  %mo +
                  %mn 2
                  %msubsup
                    %mi x
                    %mn 2
                    %mn 2
                  %mo +
                  %mn 4
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w_4(X)=x_1^4+2x_2^2+4x_4
          %p
            and in general
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:displaystyle => "true"}
                      %msub
                        %mi w
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %munder
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                        %mrow
                          %mi d
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi n
                      %msubsup
                        %mi dx
                        %mi d
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \displaystyle w_n(X)=\sum_{d|n} dx_d^{n/d}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi w
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi w
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w_n(w)
            of the
            = succeed "-th" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi w
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w\in W(k)
            of the Witt ring of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            is sometimes called the
            %em
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              \-th phantom component of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi w
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w
            or
            %em
              the
              = succeed "-th" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi w
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w
          %p
            Now let
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi z
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi z
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi z
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi z
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi(z_1, z_2)\in\mathbb{Z}[z_1, z_2]
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
          %p
            We can define new polynomials
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Φ
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi i
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi y
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %msub
                    %mi y
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi_i(x_1, \ldots x_i, y_1, \ldots y_i)
            such that the following condition is met
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi w
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi w
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi y
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi y
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi w
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Φ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi y
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi Φ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi y
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi y
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi(w_n(x_1, \ldots ,x_n), w_n(y_1, \ldots , y_n))=w_n(\Phi_1(x_1, y_1), \ldots , \Phi_n(x_1, \ldots x_n, y_1, \ldots , y_n))
          %p
            In short we’ll notate this
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi w
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi w
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi w
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Φ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi(w_n(X),w_n(Y))=w_n(\Phi(X,Y))
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_i
            can be written as a
            = succeed "-linear" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℚ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi w
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w_n
            just by some linear algebra.
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mn 1
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi w
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_1=w_1
            , and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 2
                    %mo =
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                    %msub
                      %mi w
                      %mn 2
                    %mo +
                    %mfrac
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                    %msubsup
                      %mi w
                      %mn 1
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_2=\frac{1}{2}w_2+\frac{1}{2}w_1^2
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℚ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Φ
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi_i
            are actually in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
          %h4#AdditionAndMultiplicationPolynomials The addition- and multiplication polynomials
          %p
            Define yet another set of polynomials
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_i
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Π
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi_i
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ι
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \iota_i
            by the following properties:
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi w
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi w
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi w
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w_n(\Sigma)=w_n(X)+w_n(Y)
            ,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi w
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Π
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi w
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mi w
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w_n(\Pi)=w_n(X)w_n(Y)
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi w
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ι
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msub
                      %mi w
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w_n(\iota)=-w_n(X)
          %p
            We now can construct
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(A)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(A)
            to be the set of all infinite sequences
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a_1, a_2, \ldots)
            with entries in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo +
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi Σ
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi Σ
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi b
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a_1, a_2, \ldots, )+(b_1, b_2, \ldots)=(\Sigma_1(a_1,b_1), \Sigma_2(a_1,a_2,b_1,b_2), \ldots)
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi Π
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a_1, a_2, \ldots )\cdot (b_1, b_2, \ldots )=(\Pi_1(a_1,b_1), \Pi_2(a_1,a_2,b_1,b_2), \ldots )
          %h3#DefinitionUniversalCharacterization Universal characterization
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p The assignment
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi k
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    W
                    \\;\colon\;
                    k\mapsto W(k)
            %p
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi CRing
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Λ
                    %mi Ring
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    W \;\colon\; CRing \longrightarrow \Lambda Ring
            %p
              from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+rings"} commutative rings
              to that of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lambda-rings"} Lambda-rings
            %p
              Composed with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Λ
                    %mi Ring
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi CRing
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    U \;\colon\;
                    \\Lambda Ring \longrightarrow CRing
            %p
              this is the unique
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endofunctor"} endofunctor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi CRing
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi CRing
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W \;\colon\; CRing \longrightarrow CRing
              such that all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witt+polynomials"} Witt polynomials
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi w
                      %mi n
                    %mo :
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable{:columnalign => "left left", :displaystyle => "false"}
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi W
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi A
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo →
                              %mi A
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi a
                              %mo ↦
                              %msub
                                %mi w
                                %mi n
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi a
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    w_n
                    \:
                    \\begin{cases}
                    W(A)\to A
                    \\\
                    a\mapsto w_n(a)
                    \\end{cases}
            %p
              are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphisms"} homomorphisms
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rings"} rings
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              There is a nice trick to prove that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(A)
              is a ring when
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is a
              = succeed "-algebra." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℚ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo :
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi: W(A)\to A^\mathbb{N}
              by
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ↦
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi w
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi w
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a_1, a_2, \ldots) \mapsto (w_1(a), w_2(a), \ldots)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijection"} bijection
              and the addition and multiplication is taken to component-wise addition and multiplication, so since this is the standard ring structure we know
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(A)
              is a ring. Also,
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi w
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w(0,0,\ldots)=(0,0,\ldots)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (0,0,\ldots)
              is the additive identity,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi(1,0,0,\ldots)=(1,1,1,\ldots)
              which shows
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1,0,0,\ldots)
              is the multiplicative identity, and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi w
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi ι
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi ι
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} w(\iota_1(a), \iota_2(a), \ldots)=(-a_1, -a_2, \ldots)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi ι
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi ι
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\iota_1(a), \iota_2(a), \ldots)
              is the additive inverse.
            %p
              We can actually get this idea to work for any characteristic
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
              ring by considering the embedding
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi ℚ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A\to A\otimes\mathbb{Q}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi ℚ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(A)\to W(A\otimes\mathbb{Q})
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℚ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi ℚ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(A\otimes\mathbb{Q})
              is a ring, so since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↦
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (0,0,\ldots)\mapsto (0,0,\ldots)
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↦
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1,0,0,\ldots)\mapsto (1,0,0,\ldots)
              and the map preserves inverses we get that the image of the embedding
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi ℚ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(A)\to W(A\otimes \mathbb{Q})
              is a subring and hence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(A)
              is a ring.
            %p
              Lastly, we need to prove this for positive
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic"} characteristic
              rings. Choose a characteristic
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
              ring that surjects onto
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B\to A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(B)\to W(A)
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surjective"} surjective
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(A)
              is a ring.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The construction of the ring of Witt vectors
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(k)
              on a given
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              from
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lambda-rings"} Lambda-rings
              to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+rings"} commutative rings
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi CRing
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi W
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mi U
                    %mi Λ
                    %mi Ring
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (U \dashv W)
                    \\;\colon\;
                    CRing
                    \\stackrel{\overset{U}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{W}{\longrightarrow}}
                    \\Lambda Ring
                    \\,.
            %p
              Hence rings of Witt-vectors are the
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/co-free+functors"} co-free
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lambda-rings"} Lambda-rings
          %p
            This statement appears in (
            %a{:href => "#Hazewinkel08"}> Hazewinkel 08, p. 87, p. 97
            ).
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              On the other hand, the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+construction"} free
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lambda-ring"} Lambda-ring
              (on one generator) (hence the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
              construction to the
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+functions"} symmetric functions
          %p
            This statement appears in (
            %a{:href => "#Hazewinkel08"}> Hazewinkel 08, p. 98
            ).
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#operations_on_the_padic_witt_vectors Operations on the p-adic Witt vectors
          %p
            On untruncated
            = succeed "-adic" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frobenius+morphism"} Frobenius morphism
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Verschiebung+morphism"} Verschiebung morphism
            satisfying relations (
            %a{:href => "#FVrelations"}> Lemma 1
            ) being constitutive for the definition of the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dieudonn%C3%A9+ring"} Dieudonné ring
          %p
            Also the
            = succeed "-truncation" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi W
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W_n(A)
            of a Witt ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(A)
            is a ring since by definition the first
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            components of a sum or product in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(A)
            only depend on the first
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            components of the elements being added or multiplied. We have
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi lim
                    %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mi W
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(A) \simeq lim_n W_n(A)
            and the projection map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi W
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(A)\to W_n(A)
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+homomorphism"} ring homomorphism
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W_n(A)
          %h4#the_shift_map The shift map
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(k)
            as for every
            = succeed "-scheme" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Verschiebung+morphism"} Verschiebung morphism
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frobenius+morphism"} Frobenius morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(k)
            the Verschiebung morphism coincides with the shift
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↦
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a_0, a_1,\dots)\mapsto (0, a_0, a_1,\dots)
          %p
            For the truncated Witt rings and the shift operation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi W
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi W
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V:W_n(k)\to W_{n+1}(k)
            the Verschiebung morphism equals the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi VR
                  %mo =
                  %mi RV
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} VR=RV
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is the restriction map.
          %h4#the_restriction_map The restriction map
          %p
            The restriction map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi W
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi W
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R: W_{n+1}(A)\to W_n(A)
            is given by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↦
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a_0, \ldots, a_n)\mapsto (a_0, \ldots, a_{n-1})
          %h4#the_frobenius_morphism The Frobenius morphism
          %p
            The Frobenius endomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi W
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi W
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F: W_n(A)\to W_n(A)
            is given by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↦
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi a
                      %mn 0
                      %mi p
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msubsup
                      %mi a
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                      %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a_0, \ldots , a_{n-1})\mapsto (a_0^p, \ldots, a_{n-1}^p)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is of characteristic
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
          %p
            Just by brute force checking on elements we see a few relations between these operations, namely that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi y
                  %mo =
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V(x)y=V(x F(R(y)))
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi RVF
                  %mo =
                  %mi FRV
                  %mo =
                  %mi RFV
                  %mo =
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} RVF=FRV=RFV=p
            the multiplication by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            map.
          %h3#duality_of_finite_witt_groups Duality of finite Witt groups
          %p
            For a
            = succeed "-ring" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi W
                    %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "0"}
                      %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W^\prime(R)
            denote the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ideal"} ideal
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(R)
            consisting of sequences
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x=(x_n)_n
            of nilpotent elements in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(R)
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi x
                    %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x_n=0
            for large
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            denote the
            = succeed "." do
              %span.newWikiWord
                Artin-Hasse exponential
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Artin-Hasse+exponential"} ?
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E(x,1)
            is a polynomial for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi W
                    %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "0"}
                      %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi R
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in W^\prime(R)
            and
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mrow
                    %mo {
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "left left", :displaystyle => "false"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi W
                              %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "0"}
                                %mo ′
                            %mo →
                            %msub
                              %mi μ
                              %mi k
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi w
                            %mo ↦
                            %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi w
                            %mo ,
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  E(-,1):\begin{cases}W^\prime\to \mu_k
                  
                  \\\
                  w\mapsto E(w,1)\end{cases}
          %p
            is a morphism of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+schemes"} group schemes
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multiplicative+group+scheme"} multiplicative group scheme
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi μ
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu_k
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              a)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi W
                      %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "0"}
                        %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W^\prime (R)
              is an ideal in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(R)
            %p
              b)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi W
                      %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "0"}
                        %mo ′
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi μ
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E(-,1): W^\prime\to \mu_k
              is an morphism of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+schemes"} group schemes
            %p c) The morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable{:columnalign => "left left", :displaystyle => "false"}
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi W
                              %mo ×
                              %msup
                                %mi W
                                %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "0"}
                                  %mo ′
                              %mo →
                              %msub
                                %mi μ
                                %mi k
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi x
                              %mo ,
                              %mi y
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo ↦
                              %mi E
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi xy
                              %mo ,
                              %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{cases}
                    W\times W^\prime\to \mu_k
                    \\\
                    (x,y)\mapsto E(xy,1)
                    \\end{cases}
            %p
              is bilinear and gives an isomorphism of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+schemes"} group schemes
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi W
                      %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "0"}
                        %mo ′
                    %mo →
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W^\prime\to D(W)
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              denotes the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartier+dual"} Cartier dual
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              (maybe it is equivalently the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontryagin+dual"} Pontryagin dual
              of the underlying group of the (plain) ring
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartier+dual"} Cartier dual
            %p
              d) For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in W(R)
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi W
                      %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "0"}
                        %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y\in W^\prime (R)
              we have
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi xy
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mo ×
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E(xy,1)\in R^\times
              and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi V
                      %mi n
                    %mi x
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi T
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %msup
                      %mi F
                      %mi n
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %msup
                      %mi F
                      %mi n
                    %mi y
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E(V^n x y,1)=E (T^n(x F^n y),1)=E(x F^n y,1)
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_and_theorem Definition and Theorem
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi F
                      %mi n
                      %mi m
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mi ker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi F
                      %mi m
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mi nk
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mi nk
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ker(F_n^m):=ker (F^m:W_{nk}\to W_{nk})
              denote the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel"} kernel
              of
              = succeed "-times" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frobenius+endomorphism"} Frobenius endomorphism
              of the
              = succeed "-truncated" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi σ
                      %mi n
                    %mo :
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable{:columnalign => "left left", :displaystyle => "false"}
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi W
                                %mi nk
                              %mo →
                              %msub
                                %mi W
                                %mi k
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msub
                                %mi α
                                %mn 0
                              %mo ,
                              %mi …
                              %mo ,
                              %msub
                                %mi α
                                %mrow
                                  %mi n
                                  %mo −
                                  %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo ↦
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msub
                                %mi α
                                %mn 0
                              %mo ,
                              %mi …
                              %mo ,
                              %msub
                                %mi α
                                %mrow
                                  %mi n
                                  %mo −
                                  %mn 1
                              %mo ,
                              %mn 0
                              %mo ,
                              %mi …
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\sigma_n:\begin{cases}
                    
                    W_{nk}\to W_k
                    \\\
                    (\alpha_0,\dots,\alpha_{n-1})\mapsto(\alpha_0,\dots,\alpha_{n-1},0,\dots)
                    \\end{cases}
            %p
              be the section of the restriction
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi R
                        %mi n
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi W
                        %mi k
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi W
                        %mi nk
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_n:W_k\to W_{nk}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi σ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma_n
              sends
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi F
                      %mi n
                      %mi m
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ker(F_n^m)
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi W
                        %mstyle{:scriptlevel => "0"}
                          %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W^\prime
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi σ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma_n
              is not a morphism of groups.
            %p We define the bilinear map
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mo :
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable{:columnalign => "left left", :displaystyle => "false"}
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi ker
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msubsup
                                %mi F
                                %mi n
                                %mi m
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo ×
                              %mi ker
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msubsup
                                %mi F
                                %mi m
                                %mi n
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo →
                              %msup
                                %mi R
                                %mo ×
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo &lt;
                              %mi x
                              %mo ,
                              %mi y
                              %mo &gt;
                              %mo ↦
                              %mi E
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msub
                                %mi σ
                                %mi n
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi x
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %msub
                                %mi σ
                                %mi m
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi y
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo ,
                              %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\lt-,-\gt:\begin{cases}
                    ker(F^m_n)\times ker(F^n_m)\to R^\times
                    \\\
                    \\lt x,y\gt\mapsto E(\sigma_n(x)\sigma_m(y),1)
                    \\end{cases}
            %p
              then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo &gt;
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lt x,y\gt
              is bilinear and gives an isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi F
                      %mi n
                      %mi m
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi F
                      %mi m
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ker(F^m_n)\simeq D(ker(F^n_m)
            %p and satisfies
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi t
                    %mi y
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mo =
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi f
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo &gt;
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lt x,t y\gt=\lt f x,y\gt
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi r
                    %mi y
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mo =
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi i
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo &gt;
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lt x,r y\gt=\lt i x,y\gt
            %p where the morphisms are
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ker
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msubsup
                              %mi F
                              %mi n
                              %mi m
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi t
                          %mtd
                            %mi ker
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msubsup
                              %mi F
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo +
                                %mn 1
                              %mi m
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mi r
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ker
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msubsup
                              %mi F
                              %mi n
                              %mrow
                                %mi m
                                %mo −
                                %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ↪
                              %mi i
                          %mtd
                            %mi ker
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msubsup
                              %mi F
                              %mi n
                              %mi m
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    ker(F^m_n)
                    \&amp;\stackrel{t}{\to}&amp;
                    ker(F^m_{n+1})
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow^f&amp;&amp;\downarrow^r
                    \\\
                    ker(F^{m-1}_n)
                    \&amp;\stackrel{i}{\hookrightarrow}&amp;
                    ker(F^m_n)
                    }
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              is the canonical inclusion, and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo ,
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r,f,t
              are induced by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo ,
                    %mi F
                    %mo ,
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R,F,T
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frobenius+morphism"} Frobenius
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witt+ring"} Verschiebung
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo :
                    %mi W
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R:W\to W_n
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witt+ring"} restriction
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
              are monomorphisms,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
              are epimorphisms, and for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi F
                      %mi m
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ker(F^n_m)
              we have
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo =
                    %mi if
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F=if
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                      %mo =
                      %mi rt
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V=rt
          %p
            References:
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Pink"} Pink, §25
            %a{:href => "#Demazure"} Demazure, III.4
          %h2#properties_of_the_witt_group Properties of the Witt group
          %p
            The group of universal (i.e. not
            = succeed "-adic)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                  %mo +
                  %mi X
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(k)= 1+X k [ [ X] ]
            i.e. the multiplicative group of power series in one variable
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            with constant term
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
          %h2#properties_of_the_witt_ring Properties of the Witt ring
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_2 Theorem
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              be a perfect field of prime characteristic
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %p
              Then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(k)
              is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi pW
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %msubsup
                        %mi a
                        %mn 0
                        %mi p
                      %mo ,
                      %msubsup
                        %mi a
                        %mn 1
                        %mi p
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} pW(k)=(0, a_0^p, a_1^p, \ldots )
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi pW
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(k)/pW(k)\simeq k
            %p
              Also,
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %msup
                        %mi p
                        %mi n
                      %mi W
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %msub
                        %mi W
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(k)/p^n W(k)\simeq W_n(k)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(k)
              with respect to the maximal ideal is just
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi lim
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} lim W_n(k)\simeq W(k)
              which shows that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(k)
              is a complete discrete valuation ring.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %h3#basic_examples Basic examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi W
                        %mrow
                          %msup
