          %h2#references References
          %h3#original_texts_and_classical_surveys Original texts and classical surveys
          %p Witt vectors were introduced in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ernst+Witt"}> Ernst Witt
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Zyklische Körper und Algebren der Characteristik
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                  vom Grad
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi p
                            %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^n
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi p
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^n
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.digizeitschriften.de/main/dms/img/?IDDOC=504725"} web
          %p
            In the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+group+laws"} formal group laws
            they were used in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean+Dieudonn%C3%A9"}> Jean Dieudonné
              ,
              %em
                Groupes de Lie et hyperalgèbres de Lie sur un corps de charactéristique
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo &gt;
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \gt 0
                VII“ Math. Ann. , 134 (1957) pp. 114–133
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michiel+Hazewinkel"}> Michiel Hazewinkel
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Twisted Lubin-Tate formal group laws, ramified Witt vectors and (ramified) Artin-Hasse exponentials
          %p Surveys include:
          %ul#eom
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/eom"}> eom
              ,
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://www.encyclopediaofmath.org/index.php/Witt_vector"} Witt vector
          %ul
            %li
              Michel Demazure,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Demazure%2C+lectures+on+p-divisible+groups"} Lectures on p-divisible groups
              (
              %a{:href => "http://sites.google.com/site/mtnpdivisblegroupsworkshop/lecture-notes-on-p-divisible-groups"}> web
              )
          %h3#modern_surveys Modern surveys
          %ul
            %li
              %p#Hazewinkel08
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michiel+Hazewinkel"}> Michiel Hazewinkel
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hazewinkel%2C+Witt+vectors"} Witt vectors
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0804.3888"} arXiv
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michiel+Hazewinkel"}> Michiel Hazewinkel
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Formal Groups and Applications
                %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/DPubS?service=UI&version=1.0&verb=Display&handle=euclid.bams/1183548600"} Project Euclid
            %li
              %p
                H. Lenstra, Construction of the ring of Witt vectors, Eur. J. Math (2019) 5, 1234-–1241. (
                %a{:href => "https://math.berkeley.edu/~hwl/papers/witt.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+Pink"}> Richard Pink
                , Finite group schemes, (
                %a#Pink{:href => "http://www.math.ethz.ch/~pink/ftp/FGS/CompleteNotes.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li
              %p
                Joseph Rabinoff,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The theory of Witt vectors
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1409.7445"} arXiv
            %li
              %p
                Niranjan Ramachandran, Zeta functions, Grothendieck groups, and the Witt ring, (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1407.1813"}> arXiv
                )
          %p
            A review in the context of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kummer-Artin-Schreier-Witt+exact+sequence"} Kummer-Artin-Schreier-Witt exact sequence
            is in
          %ul
            %li#MezardRomagnyTossici11
              Ariane Mézard, Matthieu Romagny, Dajano Tossici, section 2 of
              %em Sekiguchi-Suwa theory revisited
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1104.2222"}> arXiv
              )
          %h3#further_development_of_the_theory Further development of the theory
          %ul
            %li#DS88
              %p
                A. Dress, C. Siebeneicher,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Burnside ring of profinite groups and the Witt vector construction
                %a{:href => "https://reader.elsevier.com/reader/sd/pii/0001870888900527?token=448709A2504AA684DD56C07A8907E9344F0C761E77B09F8B840FF05D2E8B5338DCBBCAF713EEE9E24BCB91E2FAD4883D&originRegion=eu-west-1&originCreation=20221117110955"} link
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitri+Kaledin"}> Dmitri Kaledin
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-commutative+Witt+vectors"} non-commutative Witt vectors
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dmitri+Kaledin"}> Dmitri Kaledin
                , universal Witt vectors and the ‘’Japanese cocycle’’, (
                %a{:href => "http://imperium.lenin.ru/~kaledin/math/jap.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lars+Hesselholt"}> Lars Hesselholt
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ib+Madsen"} Ib Madsen
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mixed+characteristic"} mixed characteristic
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.uiuc.edu/K-theory/0551/paper.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lars+Hesselholt"}> Lars Hesselholt
                , Witt vectors of non-commutative rings and topological cyclic homology, (
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uiuc.edu/K-theory/0135/derived.pdf"}> pdf
                )
          %p
            In the context of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Borger%27s+absolute+geometry"} Borger's absolute geometry
          %ul
            %li#Borger08
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Borger"}> James Borger
                ,
                %em The basic geometry of Witt vectors, I: The affine case
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0801.1691"}> arXiv
                )
            %li#Borger10
              %p
